   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence at the beginning of the second paragraph to link it to the first. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rowing has been a popular sport at colleges and clubs for well over a century.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-link-to-previous"},{"text":"When one rower is early or late, the boat rocks to one side and slows down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-without-advancing"},{"text":"The coxswain is usually the lightest member of the team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Perfect timing is only part of the challenge, however, because the crew must also keep the boat on course.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Perfect timing is only part of the challenge, however, because the crew must also keep the boat on course.$q$, $q$The correct choice looks back to the timing discussed in paragraph 1 and points ahead to steering, the problem paragraph 2 solves. The sentence about rocking only repeats sentence 4 and gives no hint of the new topic.$q$, 'draft', '8dee2241-7eb3-5888-86fa-aa77b63c240f')
