insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('826efc48-60bf-59cd-8a07-6ad490e43439', 'wg10-paragraph-transitions-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Hidden Web Under the Forest$q$, $q$(1) Beneath the floor of many forests lies a vast web of fungal threads that most visitors never see. (2) These threads, called hyphae, are far thinner than a human hair, yet a single handful of forest soil can contain many meters of them. (3) Many of the fungi form partnerships with the roots of trees, wrapping around root tips or even growing inside root cells.

(4) The partnership benefits both sides. (5) The fungal threads reach into tiny spaces in the soil that roots cannot enter, gathering water and minerals such as phosphorus for the tree. (6) ____, the tree supplies the fungus with sugars it produces through photosynthesis, food the fungus cannot make for itself. (7) Because the threads can connect the roots of several neighboring trees, some scientists describe the arrangement as an underground network.

(8) Researchers have tried to measure how much material actually moves through these networks. (9) In some experiments, they have tagged carbon in one tree and later detected it in nearby seedlings. (10) ____, other researchers argue that such results are hard to interpret, because the carbon could have traveled through the soil itself rather than through the fungi. (11) The disagreement has encouraged scientists to design more careful studies before drawing broad conclusions about how forests share resources.$q$, 'draft')
