   $q$Read: "Jazz soloists often seem to invent melodies on the spot. ____, most of them have spent years practicing the scales and patterns they draw on during a performance." Which transition best completes the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Similarly,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comparison-for-contrast"},{"text":"Therefore,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"cause-for-contrast"},{"text":"In reality,","is_correct":true},{"text":"As an illustration,","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-for-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In reality,$q$, $q$The first sentence describes how soloing appears, and the second reveals what actually lies behind it, so "In reality" marks the contrast between appearance and fact. "Therefore" is wrong because seeming to invent melodies does not cause years of practice.$q$, 'draft', null)
