  ('35af8895-cae9-5e0e-85c6-e9b66b0b4227', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentences. (A) After the breeding season, the terns head south along the coasts of Europe and Africa. (B) Each spring, Arctic terns nest in the far north, raising their chicks in the long summer daylight. (C) Finally, they reach the waters near Antarctica, where it is summer once again. (D) Along the way, they stop to feed in rich ocean areas, sometimes for weeks at a time. Which order makes the paragraph most logical?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, D, C, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"C, B, A, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"A, B, D, C","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-time-order"},{"text":"B, A, D, C","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, A, D, C$q$, $q$Sentence B introduces the terns at their nesting grounds, A starts the trip south, D describes stops "along the way," and C uses "Finally" to end the journey. Starting with A fails because "the terns" and "the breeding season" need sentence B to introduce them first.$q$, 'draft', null)
