  ('07951894-5f23-5a38-b407-5604bf7698ed', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "____ Old phones contain small amounts of gold, silver, and copper in their circuits. Their batteries can be processed to recover lithium and cobalt. Even the plastic cases can be ground up and molded into new products." Which sentence best fills the blank as the topic sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Technology has changed the way people live in many different ways.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"A discarded phone is a surprisingly rich source of materials that can be used again.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many people replace their phones every two or three years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Gold is used in phone circuits because it conducts electricity well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A discarded phone is a surprisingly rich source of materials that can be used again.$q$, $q$Every supporting sentence names a part of a phone that can be recovered and reused, and the correct choice states that shared idea. The sentence about gold is tempting because it matches the first detail, but it does not cover the batteries or the plastic cases.$q$, 'draft', null)
