  ('e77e3432-b88d-59f2-9148-acafc61f0fca', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read: "The museum's new exhibit attracted record crowds. The museum had spent almost nothing on advertising." Which choice best combines these sentences to show the relationship between the ideas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The museum's new exhibit attracted record crowds because the museum had spent almost nothing on advertising.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The museum had spent almost nothing on advertising, so the new exhibit attracted record crowds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The museum's new exhibit attracted record crowds even though the museum had spent almost nothing on advertising.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The museum's new exhibit attracted record crowds, and the museum had also spent almost nothing on advertising.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"addition-hides-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The museum's new exhibit attracted record crowds even though the museum had spent almost nothing on advertising.$q$, $q$Large crowds are unexpected when a museum barely advertises, so "even though" shows the contrast between the ideas. The "because" version is tempting, but spending almost nothing on advertising would not cause crowds to grow.$q$, 'draft', null)
