  ('a0046ab2-bcce-5889-a10c-e103e63ba770', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A writer has finished a paragraph explaining how 3D printers build objects one thin layer at a time. The next paragraph explains how hospitals use 3D printing to make custom splints for injured patients. Which sentence best begins the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because this layered process can produce almost any shape, hospitals have begun using it to make splints that fit a single patient.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Hospitals treat thousands of broken wrists and ankles every year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-link-to-previous"},{"text":"Each layer of plastic is usually thinner than a sheet of paper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-without-advancing"},{"text":"In contrast to 3D printing, hospitals rely on doctors and nurses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because this layered process can produce almost any shape, hospitals have begun using it to make splints that fit a single patient.$q$, $q$The correct sentence refers back to the layered process from the first paragraph and explains how that feature leads to the hospital use in the second. The sentence about broken wrists introduces the new topic but gives no link to the printing process just described.$q$, 'draft', null)
