  ('426fa1c9-2d93-5303-b134-babf25cb7c05', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentences. (A) However, a rain garden works only if its plants are chosen carefully, since many species cannot survive both flooding and drought. (B) A rain garden is a shallow, planted hollow designed to catch water that runs off roofs and driveways. (C) Instead of rushing into storm drains, that water soaks slowly into the soil, where roots and microbes filter out pollutants. (D) For this reason, designers usually choose native plants that are adapted to the local cycle of wet and dry seasons. Which order makes the paragraph most logical?$q$, $q$[{"text":"C, B, D, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-words"},{"text":"B, C, D, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"},{"text":"B, C, A, D","is_correct":true},{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-transition-cues"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, C, A, D$q$, $q$B defines a rain garden, C explains what happens to "that water," A turns with "However" to a limitation, and D gives the solution "For this reason." Placing D before A fails because D's choice of hardy native plants answers the problem of flooding and drought that only A raises.$q$, 'draft', null)
