  ('cab8df21-8bfa-5cde-9850-444f5cacf626', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "Many desert plants survive on very little water; cacti, for example, store moisture in thick, waxy stems." What is the purpose of the phrase "for example" in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that cacti are a specific case of the general idea about desert plants.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the writer is ending the discussion of desert plants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-read-as-conclusion"},{"text":"It shows that desert plants survive because cacti store water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-read-as-cause"},{"text":"It shows that cacti are different from other desert plants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"example-read-as-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that cacti are a specific case of the general idea about desert plants.$q$, $q$"For example" signals that the cactus illustrates the broader claim that desert plants survive on little water. It does not mark a contrast, since cacti are presented as one of those plants rather than an exception.$q$, 'draft', null)
